# I-SAGIPH

**Interactive Software for Analyzing Geographic Inadequacy in Philippine Healthcare**

> The Python package and conda environment keep their original name, `isagiph`, so all commands below are unchanged.

I-SAGIPH combines public data on hospitals, population, poverty, and disease to locate cities and municipalities where healthcare need outstrips healthcare capacity. It consolidates the data into three indices: a **Health Need Index (HNI)**, a **Hospital Capacity Index (HCI)** built on E2SFCA spatial accessibility, and the **Healthcare Gap Index (HGI)**. Indicator weights come from factor analysis (Wang & Luo, 2005; OECD & JRC, 2008). It then tests where gaps cluster, checks how robust each result is, and validates the index against outcomes it was not built from. Everything is served through an interactive Streamlit map and citizen-facing navigation page.

## Quick start (5 minutes, no downloads)

```bash
git clone <repo-url> && cd isagiph
conda env create -f environment.yml && conda activate isagiph   # or: pip install -r requirements.txt && pip install -e .
python -m isagiph.pipeline --demo      # synthetic data, ~1 min
pytest -q                              # unit tests
python -m streamlit run app/app.py               # dashboard at http://localhost:8501
```

The `--demo` flag uses a **synthetic** dataset (`src/isagiph/synthetic.py`) in the same schema as the real data, so the whole pipeline can be tested and demonstrated before every source arrives. Demo numbers are not findings; the dashboard and report label them clearly.

## Running on real data

1. Copy the source files into `data/manual/` (or point `paths.manual` in `config/config.yaml` at the folder where they are) (file names may differ slightly; `build_real.py` finds them by pattern):
   `phl_admin_boundaries.xlsx`, `4_Household…2020…CPH….xlsx`, `2_2023_SAE_with_PSGC….xlsx`, the 2023 GIDA PDF,
   `Hospital_list_as_of….xlsx`, `List_of_Infirmary….xlsx`, `List_of_Primary_Care_Facilities….xlsx`,
   `Free-standing_Ambulance….xlsx`, `PCSO_Malasakit_Centers….pdf`, and `health_facilities.gpkg` (HOT OSM). For road-network routing, also place the Philippines **roads** GeoPackage in `data/manual/`. If more than one plausible roads GeoPackage exists, set `roads.file` (and optionally `roads.layer`) in `config/config.yaml` to the exact roads source. `health_facilities.gpkg` is for matching facility coordinates and is deliberately excluded from road graph selection. Travel speeds are explicit transport assumptions intended to approximate mixed local travel conditions. The modeled estimate of residents beyond 30 minutes from a hospital is reported separately from the supplied DOH reference; PHFDP 30-minute context figures refer to primary-care centres and should not be interpreted as hospital-specific measurements.
   For true city/municipality outlines on the map, also put the COD-AB boundary download (shapefile, geodatabase, GeoPackage or GeoJSON from HDX's *Philippines – Subnational Administrative Boundaries*) in `data/manual/`.
2. `python -m isagiph.build_real` links everything to COD-AB city/municipality codes and writes
   `data/interim/` plus `reports/data_quality.md` (every match rate and every unlinked record).
3. *(Recommended)* Road-network travel times as `data/interim/travel_times.csv` (see `docs/methodology.md`);
   otherwise a documented straight-line fallback is used.
4. `python -m isagiph.pipeline` writes `data/processed/` and `reports/findings.md`.
5. `python -m streamlit run app/app.py --server.headless true`.

Optional extras:

- Road travel times: put an OpenStreetMap roads GeoPackage in the source-data folder, then run `python -m isagiph.roadtimes --all` (or one region by name; `--list` shows names) and re-run the pipeline. No internet needed.
- `python -m isagiph.community` adds labelled sample posts for demos; `python -m isagiph.community --remove-samples` deletes them.

## Citizen-facing service navigation

The new **Para sa Mamamayan** page is designed for residents rather than analysts. It reuses the project facility directory to search by location and services, links to official DOH Malasakit Center directories and other public program information, provides a non-universal visit-preparation checklist, and accepts optional anonymous reports of access barriers. These reports are unverified local signals; they are not official complaints, emergency alerts, or automatically delivered to government offices. Read `docs/citizen_feature.md` for the page's data limitations and deployment considerations.

The facility directory is not live availability information. The build pipeline notes that Malasakit Center matching uses a PCSO list dated November 2022, so the page asks residents to confirm current status through the official DOH directories before travelling.

## Pipeline

```
ingest -> clean (PSGC harmonisation, facility de-dup, schema validation)
       -> accessibility (travel times, E2SFCA, coverage)
       -> indicators (age shares, DOH disease rates, primary-care density)
       -> indices (HVS, HCS, Gap Index, bivariate class, bed gap)
       -> spatial statistics (Moran's I, LISA, Gi*, FDR, constrained clustering)
       -> sensitivity (Monte Carlo) -> validation -> report + dashboard
```

## Repository layout

| Path | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `config/config.yaml` | Every analytical parameter, with comments |
| `config/sources.yaml` | Data manifest: URLs, citations, column mappings |
| `src/isagiph/ingest.py` | Downloads with checksums; manual-source checklist |
| `src/isagiph/build_real.py`, `facilities.py`, `schema.py` | Team's source files to validated standard tables |
| `src/isagiph/accessibility.py` | Travel times, E2SFCA, coverage |
| `src/isagiph/smoothing.py` | Empirical Bayes rates |
| `src/isagiph/indices.py` | HVS, HCS, Gap Index, bed gap |
| `src/isagiph/spatial_stats.py` | Moran's I, LISA, Gi*, FDR, regionalisation |
| `src/isagiph/sensitivity.py`, `validation.py` | Robustness and external validity |
| `src/isagiph/ml.py`, `equity.py`, `simulate.py`, `community.py` | Machine learning, equity statistics, what-if simulator, community storage |
| `src/isagiph/report.py`, `pipeline.py` | Findings report and orchestration |
| `app/app.py`, `app/common.py`, `app/views/`, `app/assets/`, `.streamlit/config.toml` | Multipage Streamlit dashboard. Explore: Map, Facility Finder, LGU Profile, Priority List, ISAGIP Simulator. Analyze: Regression Explorer, Health Relationships (Relationships and Equity & Fairness internal tabs), Crisis Impact. Mamamayan: Para sa Mamamayan (facility search, official assistance links, visit checklist, access-barrier reports, facility reports, and health announcements). Learn: How to Read, Data & Methods, About |
| `tests/` | Unit and smoke tests (run in CI) |
| `docs/` | Code guide, statistical models, methodology, references, data card, demo script |

